cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "HighContrastHomogenization: a Lean 4 formalization of homogenization at a polynomial scale in high contrast"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper
  "Homogenization at a polynomial scale in high contrast" (Armstrong, Kuusi,
  Loher): polynomial entry into the small-contrast regime for stationary
  coefficient fields satisfying a coarse ellipticity condition above a
  random source scale, algebraic convergence of the annealed coarse-grained
  matrices, and quantitative homogenization with correctors, a first-order
  Liouville theorem and large-scale regularity above a random scale with an
  explicit tail.  Built on the public CoarseGraining homogenization library.
  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
    affiliation: "CNRS and Laboratoire Jacques-Louis Lions, Sorbonne Université; Courant Institute of Mathematical Sciences, New York University"
  - family-names: Kuusi
